      "explanation": "Which electrode have higher value of standard reduction potential (SRP), that electrode will be strongest oxidizing agent.\n<br><br>Tendency to gain electrone is called standard reduction potential. When tendency to gain electron is more then that electrode will have more oxidizing power.\n<br><br>Here given SRP's are :\n<br><br><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.8ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"18.59ex\" height=\"2.749ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -861.5 8216.6 1215\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D438\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D438\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(848.3,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"398\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-398\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(1481.4,-176.7) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(796,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1199.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"2F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(1699.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(864,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transfor